# Malformed SIA DC-09 frames for NAK/error response testing
# These frames intentionally violate protocol rules.
# Expected behavior: NAK response or timeout (not ACK)
#
# Used by: test_harness_malformed_frame_gets_nak()
# Note: The harness treats this file specially — timeouts are not counted as failures.

# Frame 1: Missing LF start delimiter (0xFF instead of 0x0A)
# The simulator cannot locate the message — responds with NAK (unknown type)
FF 41 34 34 32 30 30 33 38 22 53 49 41 2D 44 43 53 22 30 30 30 31 4C 30 23 30 30 31 32 33 34 5B 23 30 30 31 32 33 34 7C 31 31 33 30 5D 5F 31 34 3A 32 33 3A 34 35 2C 30 34 2D 30 39 2D 32 30 32 36 0D

# Frame 2: Unknown id_token (not SIA-DCS, ACK, NAK, or NULL)
# The simulator returns NAK for unknown frame types
0A 30 30 30 30 30 30 32 32 22 42 41 44 54 4F 4B 45 4E 22 30 30 30 31 4C 30 23 30 30 31 32 33 34 5B 5D 0D

# Frame 3: Completely garbled bytes — no valid structure
# The simulator cannot parse — responds with NAK
FF FE FD FC FB FA F9 F8 F7 F6 F5 F4 F3 F2 F1 F0 EF EE ED EC EB EA E9 E8
